      "markdown": "# Top Use Cases\n\n## What Use Cases Are Customers Interested In?\n\n### Theme 1: Automated List Building & AI Prospecting\n\n**Frequency:** 11/22 transcripts across 7 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Branch, Diligent, Udemy, Movable Ink, Zone & Co) | **Confidence:** High\n\nThe dominant use case. AI agent automatically builds target account/contact lists on a recurring basis (typically weekly), with enrichment data attached, ready to push into a sales engagement platform.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Weekly automated prospecting at scale, a hundred leads per rep per week\" — TravelPerk (Seller)\n2. \"Automated weekly list building for BDR cold calling, that's the core ask\" — Diligent (Seller)\n3. \"AI prospecting plus list building with enrichment flowing into Salesforce and Gong Engage\" — Udemy (Seller)\n4. \"AI agent identifies accounts and contacts, enriches with signals, drafts messaging, pushes to Outreach\" — TravelPerk (Seller)\n\n### Theme 2: Data Enrichment & CRM/SEP Integration\n\n**Frequency:** 7/22 transcripts across 6 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Branch, Udemy, Optimizely, Zone & Co) | **Confidence:** High\n\nCustomers call out the need for enrichment (contact data, technographics, intent signals) and seamless integration into Salesforce and sales engagement platforms. CRM cleanup and automated contact creation are recurring sub-themes.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Lead gen plus enrichment flowing into Outreach, and Salesforce campaign attribution\" — Mixpanel (Seller)\n2. \"CRM integration for automated contact creation plus Outreach sequencing\" — TravelPerk (Customer)\n3. \"Automated outbound list building, data enrichment, Demandbase operationalization\" — Branch (Seller)\n4. \"Contact enrichment, outbound support, gifting triggered by job changes\" — Zone & Co (Customer)\n\n### Theme 3: Multi-Channel Outbound Execution (Email, Phone, LinkedIn)\n\n**Frequency:** 5/22 transcripts across 4 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Branch, Diligent) | **Confidence:** High\n\nOutbound execution across multiple channels — not just email. Phone/cold calling, LinkedIn connection requests, and LinkedIn ads are explicitly mentioned.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Multi-channel outbound — email, LinkedIn ads, LinkedIn connection requests, cold calling via Nooks\" — Mixpanel (Customer)\n2. \"Strategic pivot to simpler play-based sequencing, BDR phone and LinkedIn over email\" — Mixpanel (Seller)\n3. \"Phone connection optimization, that's where they pivoted to TitanX\" — Diligent (Seller)\n\n### Theme 4: Account Prioritization & Intent Scoring\n\n**Frequency:** 4/22 transcripts across 2 opportunities (Workato, Optimizely) | **Confidence:** Medium\n\nScoring and ranking accounts using technographics, growth signals, and CIO presence. Includes unifying multiple scoring models and surfacing unassigned accounts.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Update intent scoring model plus job change campaign for enterprise targets\" — Workato (Customer)\n2. \"Separate enterprise scoring model with technographics, CIO presence, growth rate\" — Workato (Seller)\n3. \"Account prioritization plus finding the right people from CRM and LinkedIn\" — Optimizely (Customer)\n4. \"Unified cross-model account prioritization, unassigned account surfacing, CRM cleanup\" — Optimizely (Seller)\n\n### Theme 5: AI-Personalized Messaging & Outreach Drafting\n\n**Frequency:** 3/22 transcripts across 3 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Movable Ink) | **Confidence:** Medium\n\nAI drafts personalized outreach messages using buyer signals and persona mapping, including handling lower-tier accounts with AI-generated outreach.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Agent-powered personalized outbound email using signals plus persona mapping\" — Mixpanel (Seller)\n2. \"AI agent drafts messaging based on enriched signals, pushes directly to Outreach\" — TravelPerk (Seller)\n3. \"AI account research and targeting, handle lower-tier outreach automatically\" — Movable Ink (Customer)\n\n### Theme 6: Closed-Lost Re-engagement & Win-Back Plays\n\n**Frequency:** 3/22 transcripts across 3 opportunities (Mixpanel, TravelPerk, Branch) | **Confidence:** Medium\n\nUsing AI to mine closed-lost opportunities (often via Gong call transcript analysis) to identify re-engagement signals and run win-back campaigns.\n\n**Evidence:**\n\n1. \"Closed-loss re-engagement via call transcripts, mining those for signals\" — Mixpanel (Customer)\n2. \"AI lead gen plus closed-lost re-engagement via Gong transcript analysis\" — TravelPerk (Seller)\n3. \"Closed-loss play, tech rip-and-replace targeting competitive displacements\" — Branch (Seller)\n\n## Emerging and Weak Signals\n\n- **Speed-to-Value / Rapid Time-to-First-Lead** (1 transcript — Mixpanel): \"48-hour lead generation\" as proof point.\n- **Messaging Framework Simplification** (1 transcript — Mixpanel): Product simplifies how messaging is built.\n- **Pricing as Competitive Lever** (1 transcript — Udemy): Pricing model positioned as weapon against incumbents.\n- **Unlimited Predictive Models** (1 transcript — Zone & Co): Unlimited model capacity as differentiator.\n\n## How the Use Cases Connect\n\n**Use cases form a natural funnel:** Account Prioritization → Automated List Building → Data Enrichment & CRM Integration → AI-Personalized Messaging → Multi-Channel Outbound Execution. Most customers want 2-3 capabilities bundled, with list building as the anchor (7/9 opps).\n"
    },
