    {
      "id": "q2-field-marketing",
      "name": "Top Case Studies",
      "tab": "sources",
      "linked": false,
      "type": "Slides",
      "size": "12.8 MB",
      "fileType": "slide",
      "learnedOn": "2026-07-21",
      "updatedAt": "July 21",
      "updatedBy": "Hunter",
      "markdown": "# Q2 Field Marketing\n\nOur Q2 field-marketing plan focuses on the accounts that are most likely to move from consideration to evaluation this quarter. Every event, dinner, and executive briefing on this page is aimed at a specific set of accounts and a specific buying moment.\n\n## Priority Segments\n\nQ2 concentrates spend on three segments where the pipeline is strongest and the buying committee is most active:\n\n- **Financial Services** — 40% of budget. Focus on the top 25 named accounts.\n- **Manufacturing** — 35% of budget. Focus on plant-modernization deals.\n- **Healthcare and Life Sciences** — 25% of budget. Focus on the mid-market segment.\n\nAccounts outside these three segments still receive nurture and digital touches, but no field-marketing spend.\n\n## Signature Events\n\n### Executive Roundtable Series\n\nThree cities in Q2 — New York, Chicago, and San Francisco. Each roundtable seats 12 executives, hosted by a customer speaker plus a Salesforce leader. Invitations are curated jointly by the AE and the field-marketing partner.\n\n### Industry Summits\n\nWe are exhibiting at four industry events this quarter. Field-marketing owns booth logistics; AEs own the account list. Every booth staffer runs the shared *Discovery Conversation Guide* to keep messaging consistent.\n\n### Custom Dinners\n\nUp to 15 custom dinners are available for AE-nominated accounts. Each dinner requires an account plan showing at least one active opportunity or a documented executive sponsor.\n\n## Nomination Process\n\nAEs nominate accounts through the shared field-marketing portal. Every nomination captures:\n\n1. Account name and industry\n2. Opportunity stage and expected close date\n3. Named champion and economic buyer\n4. The specific event or asset requested\n5. The business outcome the seller expects from the touch\n\nNominations are reviewed weekly. Approvals are prioritized by pipeline stage, buying-committee depth, and how recently the account was last touched by field.\n\n## Measuring Success\n\nWe measure Q2 field motion on three signals: sourced pipeline, influenced pipeline, and net-new executive contacts added to targeted accounts. Weekly readouts are posted to the *field-marketing-q2* channel every Friday.\n"
    },
