    {
      "id": "high-intent-accounts",
      "name": "high-intent-accounts",
      "hidden": true,
      "type": "Document",
      "fileType": "txt",
      "updatedAt": "June 3",
      "updatedBy": "Hunter",
      "markdown": "# High-Intent Accounts\n\nA high-intent account is one where the buying committee has demonstrated recent, sustained interest in evaluating a solution. This document defines the signals we use, the thresholds that qualify an account as high-intent, and the plays the seller runs when an account crosses the line.\n\n## Signal Categories\n\nWe group intent signals into four categories. An account can qualify on any single category or a mix.\n\n### First-party Signals\n\n- Repeat product-page views by two or more contacts in the same 14-day window\n- Pricing-page views within the last 7 days\n- Return visits after downloading a `technical brief` or `security overview`\n- Attendance at a Salesforce-hosted event in the last 30 days\n\n### Third-party Signals\n\n- Sustained topic surges on 6sense, Bombora, or G2 in the account's industry taxonomy\n- Named competitor evaluations flagged by our win-loss vendor\n- Job postings that reference our category or a common displacement pattern\n\n### Relationship Signals\n\n- Meetings booked by two or more contacts inside the account in the last 30 days\n- New executive follows on the customer's leadership on LinkedIn\n- Positive replies from the champion inside the last cadence\n\n### Deal Signals\n\n- Any opportunity currently in *Discovery* or *Solution Design* with an economic buyer identified\n- A closed-lost deal within the last 12 months that is now re-engaging\n\n## Qualification Threshold\n\nAn account is considered high-intent when it accumulates **at least four signals across at least two categories** in a rolling 30-day window. Signals older than 30 days are dropped from the score so the definition reflects current momentum, not historical activity.\n\n## Plays We Run\n\n1. Notify the AE and the field-marketing partner within one business day\n2. Prioritize the account for the next available executive briefing\n3. Adjust the seller's outreach cadence to *Accelerated High-Intent* (7 touches over 10 days)\n4. Route the account to the top of the *Ready to Review* queue\n\nHigh-intent status expires 45 days after the last qualifying signal. Sellers can extend the window manually with a documented reason (for example, a scheduled executive meeting).\n\n## What This Definition Excludes\n\nHigh-intent is **not** a lead score. It says nothing about long-term account fit. Fit and intent are scored independently so the seller can prioritize accounts that are both a good fit *and* actively evaluating.\n"
    }
